---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import { links } from '../config/links';

const title = 'Technical working group';
const lead =
  'A forum for members to work through the harder measurement and implementation questions — and the Society’s channel for coordinated practitioner input to the SEEA update.';
---

<Page title={title} eyebrow="Programme" lead={lead}>
  <p class="lead">
    The technical working group is where the Society does its detailed work. It is a forum for
    members to work through more complex measurement and implementation questions, and a channel for
    coordinated practitioner input to the SEEA Central Framework update, including the global
    consultations scheduled through 2026.
  </p>

  <h2>The SEEA as reference point, not boundary</h2>
  <p>
    The Society's technical work is anchored in the <a href={links.seea} rel="noopener">SEEA</a> while
    engaging constructively with related public, corporate and community sector frameworks. The SEEA
    is the Society's principal technical reference point rather than a boundary on valid activity.
  </p>

  <h2>Terms of reference</h2>
  <p>The group's terms of reference will set out:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>who may participate;</li>
    <li>how topics are selected;</li>
    <li>the outputs the group is expected to produce;</li>
    <li>how positions or submissions are approved;</li>
    <li>whether dissenting views may be recorded; and</li>
    <li>the relationship between the group and the Society's committee.</li>
  </ul>

  <Callout tone="pending" title="In preparation">
    <p>
      The terms of reference are being drafted, and the group's leadership will be confirmed by the
      founding committee. Members who register their interest will be notified when they are
      published.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Topic-based groups over time</h2>
  <p>
    The technical programme could support topic-based groups — for example on ecosystem accounting,
    water, oceans, corporate applications, valuation, data quality, and the use of accounts in
    policy. These should emerge from member demand rather than all being promised at launch.
  </p>

  <h2>Taking part</h2>
  <p>
    Participation is open to members. Register your interest and we will contact you when the group
    convenes.
  </p>
  <p>
    <Cta href={links.expressInterest} variant="primary">
      Express interest in the technical working group
    </Cta>
  </p>
  <p class="text-small text-muted">
    Not yet a member? <a href="/membership/">Join the Society</a> first — working groups are a
    member benefit.
  </p>
</Page>
